// A full-power throw up and to the right flies a ballistic arc: it rises about 7 tiles (1.8 m), comes
// down about 25 tiles (6 m) out, bounces, skids a little and falls asleep. The thrower can't catch it.
map
BBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBB
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#...@......................................................#
############################################################
end
give Stone 3
throw 2 Stone 1 -1 1
expect 2 inv:Stone == 2
expect 2 items:Stone == 1
// rising, then the apex (above 6.5 tiles), then falling
expect 10 ivy:Stone < 0
expect 17 iy:Stone < -6.5
expect 30 ivy:Stone > 0
// it lands well out, bounces off the stone floor, and comes to rest within a few tiles of the landing
expect 37 ix:Stone > 23
expect 37 ivy:Stone < -10
expect 90 irest:Stone == 1
expect 90 ix:Stone > 25
expect 90 ix:Stone < 31
expect 90 iy:Stone > -0.2
// a weaker throw falls shorter
throw 100 Stone 1 -1 0
expect 190 items:Stone == 2
// walk over to them: resting items are picked up by walking past (both back in the pack)
hold 200-330 right
expect 330 items:Stone == 0
expect 330 inv:Stone == 3
